<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03Z9">Corollary <span data-tag="03Z9">8.5.1.33</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category. Then composition with the retraction diagram of Notation <a data-tag="03Z3" href="/tag/03Z3">8.5.1.27</a> induces a fully faithful functor $\operatorname{Fun}( \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{Ret}), \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}( \Delta ^2, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$, whose essential image is spanned by those diagrams </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ &amp;  X \ar [dr]^{r} &amp;  \\ Y \ar [ur]^{i} \ar [rr]^{ u} &amp;  &amp;  Y' } \]
</div>
<p> where $u$ is an isomorphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Corollary <a data-tag="03Z7" href="/tag/03Z7">8.5.1.31</a> with Remark <a data-tag="03Z5" href="/tag/03Z5">8.5.1.29</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
